      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. What about Fault Recording registers (whose offset and count are specified in bits 33:24 and 47:40 of the CAP register)?\n\nIn `dmar_fault()`:\n```\n\treg \u003d cap_fault_reg_offset(iommu-\u003ecap);\n\t...\n\t\tdata \u003d dmar_readl(iommu, reg +\n\t\t\t\tfault_index * PRIMARY_FAULT_REG_LEN + 12);\n\t\tif (!(data \u0026 DMA_FRCD_F))\n\t\t\tbreak;\n```\n\nand so on.\n\nSo I guess DMAR fault logging is not workable with these patches?\n\n2. What about various registers that can be read via debugfs, in `iommu_regset_show()`? I guess with these patches we get a bunch of \"iommu_mmio_read failed\" logs in dmesg whenever we read `/sys/kernel/debug/iommu/intel/iommu_regset`, and we get some random values dumped instead of the actual register values?\n\nSo if there are no security implications of _reading_ any of those registers, maybe we should just allow reading them all?",
      "revId": "57a581f055a12e9862b8c9b53e834c94b8ae5061",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
