      "message": "\u003e So I guess DMAR fault logging is not workable with these patches?\n\nFWIW, indeed:\n\n```\n\u003c3\u003e[  116.940937][    C2] DMAR: DRHD: handling fault status reg 3\n\u003c3\u003e[  116.947507][    C2] DMAR: pkvm_readl: iommu_mmio_read(reg_phys: fed91000, off: 40c) failed(err\u003d-1)\n```\n\n(used the hack aosp/3887221 to force DMA e.g. at pvmfw address, with `iommu.passthrough\u003d1`, in order to trigger a DMAR fault due to pKVM\u0027s memory protection enforcement).\n\n\u003e I guess with these patches we get a bunch of \"iommu_mmio_read failed\" logs in dmesg whenever we read /sys/kernel/debug/iommu/intel/iommu_regset\n\nFWIW, indeed we do.",
